+# 30000644: reduction maps for special polynomial automorphisms
+
+**Already solved by van den Essen, Maubach and Vénéreau in 2007.** No campaign discovery credit is claimed.
+
+The original OWR page states the affirmative answer immediately after the extracted question. `KNOWN_THEOREM.md` records the citation and a self-contained verification for arbitrary commutative Q-algebras and all finite m,n. `SOURCE_AUDIT.md` separates the recovered original report, exact published theorem metadata, and the unavailable full JPAA article.
+
+Independent source/proof review passed; see `review/REVIEW.md` (142 independent exact controls). The 211 exact controls in `verify.py` pass (SymPy 1.14.0); these supplement the all-ring proof rather than replacing it. Run `python3 verify.py` to rewrite the receipt in `verification.json`.
+
+Recommended queue status: **already_solved**, no novelty claim. Actual model: gpt-6-astra, xhigh. Zero fresh proof-search attempts; one credited reconstruction/validation activity is documented. No continued search after the known result was confirmed.
