+{
+  "id": 30000644,
+  "problem_number": "OWR-1452-008",
+  "title": "Surjectivity of Reduction Maps for Special Polynomial Automorphisms",
+  "statement": "For a commutative ring $R$ containing $\\mathbb{Q}$, $m\\geq1$, and $Y=(y_1,\\ldots,y_n)$, is the reduction map $\\operatorname{SAut}_{R[t]}(R[t][Y])\\to\\operatorname{SAut}_{R[t]/(t^m)}(R[t]/(t^m)[Y])$ surjective, where $\\operatorname{SAut}$ denotes polynomial automorphisms with Jacobian determinant $1$?",
+  "background": "Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\n\n**Source report:** [Affine Algebraic Geometry (2007), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/01, pp. 5--82](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/01)\n\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-21)\n\n**Status:** open\n\n**Assessment.** The report presents this extracted claim as an open problem, conjecture, or unresolved research direction; targeted literature checking found no authoritative complete resolution as of 2026-08-21.\n\n**Sources checked.**\n\n- [Affine Algebraic Geometry (2007), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/01, pp. 5--82](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/01)\n\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.",
